comparison: TX-23-00042 (HIGH priority, 160th District) took **37 months to judgment** then **89 days to OOS**; TX-25-00492 (LOW priority) took **14 months to judgment**. Under Judge Ginsberg in 160th District Court, we can anticipate 14-37 months before judgment depending on case complexity and service completion. The unserved status may extend timeline significantly—service must be completed before proceedings advance. This early-stage case (Day 0) provides maximum negotiation window before judgment liens attach. Estimated judgment date: **July 2027 to June 2029** range, with post-judgment OOS adding 3+ months if following HIGH benchmark patterns.\n\n## Acquisition Strategy\n**Initial Contact:** Door-knock campaign at 1607 Denton Drive within next 14 days while owners remain unserved and unaware of case severity. Deploy field acquisition specialist for face-to-face negotiation, emphasizing pre-judgment resolution benefits. **Follow-up:** If no contact after 2 door-knock attempts, initiate direct mail sequence (letter 1: settlement offer, letter 2: consequence education, letter 3: final opportunity). **Offer Range:** Open at 40-50% of assessed value (pending tax research) covering back taxes plus $8K-15K owner equity, escalating to 65% maximum if property shows strong comps and owner demonstrates willingness to negotiate. Structure as cash close within 21 days to emphasize urgency and simplicity. Highlight avoidance','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01T23:57:56.120068','2026-07-05T22:35:40.181892','2026-07-04T20:03:03.927253',1,'individual','high','BEING 0.3184 ACRES, MORE OR LESS, TRACT 19, OF THE MARTHA P. GREEN SURVEY, ABSTRACT 519, PAGE 255, AKA 1607 N. DENTON DRIVE, CITY OF CARROLLTON, TEXAS AS RECORDED IN INSTRUMENT 202300177640, OF THE DALLAS COUNTY DEED RECORDS',NULL);
INSERT INTO cases VALUES(28,'TX-26-00994','191st District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2026-05-19','OPEN','TAX DELINQUENCY','ANTONIO GRANADOS SOLORZANO','[{"name": "ANTONIO GRANADOS SOLORZANO", "address": "4632 BUNNY LANE, WYLIE, TX 75098", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "constable", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Served 06/05/2026 by Constable #2"}, {"name": "MARIA DELOSANGELES GRANADOS PINON", "address": "1018 GREENBRIAR DRIVE, GARLAND, TX 75043", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "constable", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Executed citation 06/09/2026; Made payments totaling $546.00"}]','4660 STONEWALL COVE, TEXAS',NULL,'35507','LGBS (Linebarger)','REECE, LINDA D.',4370.3900000000004411,2022,'[2022, 2023, 2024, 2025]',2,0,0,'[]',0,0,0,'','low',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,0,'2027-01-27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "GARLAND INDEPENDENT SCHOOL DISTRICT", "taxAmt": 2444.26, "penaltyInterest": 1576.13, "total": 4020.39}]',replace('# ACQUISITION MEMO: PC PEAK DEVELOPMENT\n**Case TX-26-00994 | 4660 Stonewall Cove, Texas**\n\n## Owner Situation and Debt\n\nPrimary defendant Antonio Granados Solorzano resides at 4632 Bunny Lane in Wylie, TX and was served by constable on 06/05/2026. Co-defendant Maria Delosangeles Granados Pinon resides separately at 1018 Greenbriar Drive in Garland, indicating potential separation or marital issues. Maria has demonstrated willingness to engage by making payments totaling $546.00, suggesting financial hardship but motivation to resolve the debt. The property is 0.3326 acres in the Stonewall Cove Addition. Both parties have been properly served via constable, and the case remains open with no judgment entered yet. The separated living arrangements and partial payment history indicate owners are under financial stress but may be approachable before judgment.\n\n## Timeline Analysis vs Benchmarks\n\nCase TX-26-00994 was filed on 05/19/2026 and is currently at approximately 1 month pre-judgment. Compared to benchmark HIGH priority case TX-23-00042 (37 months to judgment, 89 days to OOS), and LOW priority case TX-25-00492 (14 months to judgment), this case is in early stages with Judge Ginsberg presiding in 191st District Court. Given typical timelines in this jurisdiction, we anticipate 12-18 months until judgment if current trajectory continues. The separated defendants and partial payment activity suggest potential for resolution prior to judgment, making this a time-sensitive acquisition opportunity while owners still have equity motivation and before foreclosure sale erodes negotiating position.\n\n## Acquisition Strategy\n\n**PRIORITY: MEDIUM-HIGH** - Door knock Antonio at 4632 Bunny Lane, Wylie first (primary owner, male decision-maker likely), then Maria at 1018 Greenbriar Drive if no contact within 48 hours. Offer range: **$38,000-$52,000** depending on property condition, liens, and tax arrears. Lead with solving their HOA/tax problem and avoiding judgment on their credit. If no answer after 2 door knocks (morning and evening), send personalized direct mail to both addresses within 5 days referencing "your property at 4660 Stonewall Cove" and offering free consultation. Maria''s payment history shows she''s responsive - she may be more motivated to sell than Antonio. Follow up with both parties; the separation creates opportunity for one party to push for quick resolution.','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-04T20:03:57.463645','2026-07-05T22:35:40.181393','2026-07-04T20:03:57.463645',1,'individual','high','BEING 0.3326 ACRES, MORE OR LESS, STONEWALL COVE ADDITION, AKA 4660 STONEWALL COVE, TEXAS AS RECORDED IN INSTRUMENT 202100337164, OF THE DALLAS COUNTY DEED RECORDS.',NULL);
