District Court typically runs closer to LOW benchmarks. Conservative acquisition window: **18-24 months** before significant legal pressure. Personal service completed early (21 days post-filing) suggests Linebarger will prosecute aggressively.\n\n## ACQUISITION STRATEGY\n\n**Contact Method:** Door knock primary residence at 1491 Red Wolf Drive, Rockwall during weekday evenings (6-7pm). If no contact after 3 attempts over 10 days, send direct mail to both Rockwall and property address. **Offer Range:** $85,000-$105,000 cash (assuming $150K-$180K ARV for Westchester Estates). Lead with assumable debt payoff + $15K-$25K cash to owner, emphasizing "solve your tax problem and walk away with money." Position as immediate relief from $10,762 liability growing at 12%+ annually. Individual owners respond well to certainty and timeline—emphasize 14-day close. If resistance, pivot to lease-option structure allowing her to salvage credit while exiting tax burden.','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-04T20:04:49.070824','2026-07-05T22:35:40.184556','2026-07-04T20:04:49.070824',1,'individual','high','LOT 16, BLOCK C, WESTCHESTER ESTATES NO. 2 ADDITION, AS RECORDED IN VOLUME 93228, PAGE 2161, OF THE DALLAS COUNTY DEED RECORDS',NULL);
INSERT INTO cases VALUES(30,'TX-26-00009','192nd District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2026-01-05','OPEN','TAX DELINQUENCY','LUCY MARILYN ROGERS','[{"name": "Lucy Marilyn Rogers", "address": "5343 Marvin D Love Fwy., Apt. 151, Dallas, TX 75232-2281", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "Private Process Server", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Two citation attempts unserved (01/08/2026 and 06/23/2026)"}, {"name": "Unknown heirs, successors and assigns of Lucy Marilyn Rogers", "address": "Unknown", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Identity and location unknown"}, {"name": "Unknown owners", "address": "Unknown", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Unknown owner''s heirs, successors and assigns"}, {"name": "Any and all other persons, including adverse claimants", "address": "Unknown", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Owning or claiming legal or equitable interest in or lien upon the property"}]','',NULL,'00000303256000000','LGBS (Linebarger)','ZOKAIE, CHEYENNE MATHEW',NULL,NULL,'[]',4,0,0,'[]',1,0,0,'Multiple unserved citation attempts - defendant not located at address','high','Single defendant, known address, 7 years delinquent (within 8-year threshold), no prior suits indicated',NULL,'none',NULL,0,'2026-09-30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[]',replace('# ACQUISITION MEMO: PC PEAK DEVELOPMENT\n\n**Property:** 5343 Marvin D Love Fwy., Apt. 151, Dallas, TX 75232-2281  \n**Case:** TX-26-00009 | 192nd District Court | Judge Ginsberg, Carl  \n**Owner:** Lucy Marilyn Rogers (Individual)  \n**Filed:** January 5, 2026 | **Status:** Open, Pre-Judgment\n\n---\n\n## OWNER SITUATION & DEBT\n\nLucy Marilyn Rogers is an individual property owner facing tax foreclosure on an apartment unit. The case includes multiple unknown defendants (heirs, successors, assigns, and adverse claimants), suggesting potential title complexity or estate issues. Ms. Rogers has been unserved despite two citation attempts via private process server (01/08/2026 and 06/23/2026), indicating she may have vacated the property, be avoiding service, or the address may be incorrect. The property appears to be a condo/apartment unit based on the suite number, which typically carries lower tax liability but may involve HOA debt. Exact tax debt amount not provided but filing in 2026 suggests delinquency likely spans 2023-2025 tax years.\n\n## TIMELINE ANALYSIS vs. BENCHMARKS\n\nCurrent case age: **6 months from filing** (Jan 2026 - July 2026). Benchmark TX-23-00042 (HIGH priority) took **37 months to judgment, then 89 days to Sheriff Sale**—total 40 months. Benchmark TX-25-00492 (LOW priority) currently at **14 months to judgment** with no sale date. TX-26-00009 is tracking significantly slower than both benchmarks due to service failures. Given Judge Ginsberg''s typical timeline and the unserved status of the primary defendant after 6 months, we estimate **24-30 months to judgment** assuming service is eventually completed (late 2027/early 2028), then **60-90 days to Sheriff Sale** (Q2 2028). This extended timeline creates acquisition opportunity before service is perfected or default judgment entered.\n\n## ACQUISITION STRATEGY\n\n**Contact Method:** Door knock 5343 Marvin D Love Fwy., Apt. 151 **first** (verify occupancy/ownership despite service failures), followed by direct mail to same address and skip trace for alternative addresses. Check with apartment management for forwarding information. **Offer Range:** $8,500-$15,000 depending on tax debt verification and HOA assessment. Given condo/apartment status, assume $3,000-$7,000 in tax debt plus potential HOA','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-05T22:35:40.175584','2026-07-05T23:14:28.109279','2026-07-05T23:14:28.109279',1,'individual','high','',NULL);
INSERT INTO cases VALUES(31,'TX-23-00244','14th District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2023-02-16','OPEN','TAX DELINQUENCY','ANNIE PEARL HATLEY','[{"name": "ANNIE PEARL HATLEY", "address": "", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "citation by posting", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Served 04/17/2023 via CBP by Constable 1"}, {"name": "WILLIE JOE HATLEY", "address": "", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "citation by posting", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Served 04/17/2023 via CBP by Constable 1"}, {"name": "MARY LUCINDA HATLEY", "address": "", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "citation by posting", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Served 04/17/2023 via CBP by Constable 1"}, {"name": "PATRICIA ANN CAMP", "address": "", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Unexecuted citation returned 04/11/2023"}, {"name": "DELORES MILES MARTINEZ", "address": "", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Return unserved 05/08/2023"}, {"name": "LARRY DARNELL MILES", "address": "", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "SOS", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Served 04/03/2023 via SOS"}, {"name": "BOBBY CHARLES MILES", "address": "", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Return unserved"}, {"name": "TONY J. HATLEY", "address": "", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Return unserved"}, {"name": "TONETTE HATLEY", "address": "", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Return unserved 05/09/2023"}, {"name": "SHERRY HATLEY SADDLER", "address": "", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Return unserved 05/30/2023"}, {"name": "CORA TAYLOR PRIDE", "address": "", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Return unserved 05/30/2023"}, {"name": "CHARLOTTE RUTH WINSETT", "address": "", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Return unserved 04/11/2023"}]','',NULL,'','LGBS (Linebarger)','ATKINS, ASHLY STEELE',NULL,NULL,'[]',12,1,0,'[]',1,0,2,'Multiple defendants unserved; CBP used for 3 defendants; Attorney Ad Litem appointed','high','12 defendants (5+ triggers high complexity); multiple defendants with address unknown at filing requiring Citation by Posting; estate/heir situation evident from multiple family members and prior related 1984 suit; 20 years of delinquent taxes (2003-2022); out-of-state defendant requiring SOS service; incarcerated defendant; multiple ad litem appointments; Rule 106 substitute service needed; 3 continuances and 2 trial resets; judgment vacated requiring case reopening','2025-05-05','JUDGMENT NON-JURY',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[]',replace('# ACQUISITION MEMO: PC PEAK DEVELOPMENT\n\n**Property:** TX-23-00244 | **Owner Type:** Individual | **Primary Contact:** ANNIE PEARL HATLEY\n\n---\n\n## OWNER SITUATION & DEBT\n\nMultiple individual defendants in foreclosure action filed 02/16/2023 in 14th District Court under Judge Ginsberg. Primary defendants include ANNIE PEARL HATLEY, WILLIE JOE HATLEY, and MARY LUCINDA HATLEY (all served via citation by posting 04/17/2023). PATRICIA ANN CAMP remains unserved with unexecuted citation as of 04/11/2023. Case proceeded to non-jury judgment on 05/05/2025, indicating likely family ownership with estate/heirship complications given multiple defendants with shared surname and service by posting method. The unserved defendant and posting service suggest potential absentee ownership, unclear title, or difficulty locating all parties with interest in the property.\n\n## TIMELINE ANALYSIS VS BENCHMARKS\n\nCurrent case timeline: 27 months filed-to-judgment (F->J), significantly faster than TX-23-00042 HIGH benchmark of 37mo->J but slower than TX-25-00492 LOW benchmark of 14mo->J. Judgment entered 05/05/2025, making property approximately 89 days post-judgment. This aligns closely with TX-23-00042''s 89d->OOS (order of sale) timeline, suggesting imminent foreclosure sale scheduling within 30-60 days. Case velocity indicates moderate court processing speed with active plaintiff pursuit despite service complications. Window for pre-foreclosure acquisition closing rapidly with likely sheriff sale posting expected within next 45 days.\n\n## ACQUISITION STRATEGY\n\n**Approach Sequence:** (1) Door knock primary address for ANNIE PEARL HATLEY within 5 business days; (2) Leave door hanger with 24-hour response request if no contact; (3) Follow with personalized direct mail to all served defendants within 48 hours emphasizing judgment status and foreclosure timeline; (4) Secondary mail drop at +7 days with specific cash offer. **Offer Range:** Start 40-45% ARV given judgment complications and multiple ownership parties requiring consensus; maximum 55% ARV if clear title path and motivated sellers. Emphasize fast close (14-21 days), all cash, and resolution of family property burden. Address unserved defendant (CAMP) as title curative issue requiring 5-8% holdback or quiet title budget in acquisition analysis.','\n',char(10)),NULL,'judgment_entered',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-05T22:35:40.179547','2026-07-05T23:10:40.323379','2026-07-05T23:10:40.323379',1,'individual','high','',NULL);
INSERT INTO cases VALUES(32,'TX-25-01483','101st District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2025-09-15','OPEN','TAX DELINQUENCY','HENRY ALEXANDER BORG, JR.','[{"name": "HENRY ALEXANDER BORG, JR.", "address": "1116 Hidden Meadow Dr., Burleson, TX 76025", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "mail attorney", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "In Personam as to Tax Years 2021-2024. Answer filed 10/08/2025"}, {"name": "JAMIE CORNEJO (A/K/A JAIME CORNEJO)", "address": "1530 E. Overton Rd., Dallas, TX 75216", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "private process server", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Life Estate Only. Unexecuted citation 10/24/2025"}, {"name": "REFUGIO S. ULLOA", "address": "1526 Garza Ave., Dallas, TX 75216", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "Rule 106 substitute service", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Rule 106 order granted 11/10/2025, served 12/10/2025"}, {"name": "CIRILO S. UYOA", "address": "1349 Little Ave., Columbus, OH 43223", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "citation", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Executed citation 11/05/2025. Out of state \u2014 Ohio"}, {"name": "JOEL UYOA", "address": "3647 Desert Dr., Saginaw, MI 48603", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "private process server", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Unexecuted citation 11/12/2025. Out of state \u2014 Michigan"}, {"name": "JESSICA PONCE", "address": "1530 E. Overton Rd., Dallas, TX 75216", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "private process server", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Unexecuted citation 10/24/2025"}, {"name": "ARANZA PONCE", "address": "149 Oak Village Cir., Duncanville, TX 75137", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "private process server", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Unexecuted citation 11/11/2025. Rule 106 motion filed 12/16/2025"}]','1530 E. Overton Rd., Dallas, TX 75216-5506',NULL,'00000302749000000','LGBS (Linebarger)','ATKINS, ASHLY STEELE',16309.24999999999958,2020,'[2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024]',7,0,1,'[]',1,0,1,'Multiple defendants unserved; Rule 106 substitute service granted for Refugio Ulloa and pending for Aranza Ponce; life estate situation with Jamie Cornejo','high','7 defendants with life estate and in rem claims; multiple unexecuted citations requiring Rule 106 substitute service (2 defendants); Citation by Posting affidavits filed for 3 defendants (Jamie Cornejo, Joel Uyoa, Jessica Ponce); ad litem appointments; estate/heir complications with life estate holder; 1 continuance and 1 trial reset',NULL,'none',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "DALLAS COUNTY", "taxAmt": 1532.55, "penaltyInterest": 932.87, "total": 2465.42}, {"entity": "DALLAS INDEPENDENT SCHOOL DISTRICT", "taxAmt": 6969.53, "penaltyInterest": 4269.03, "total": 11238.56}, {"entity": "CITY OF DALLAS", "taxAmt": 1151.13, "penaltyInterest": 700.04, "total": 1851.17}, {"entity": "PARKLAND HOSPITAL DISTRICT", "taxAmt": 319.84, "penaltyInterest": 194.19, "total": 514.03}, {"entity": "DALLAS COLLEGE", "taxAmt": 156.23, "penaltyInterest": 94.84, "total": 251.07}, {"entity": "DALLAS COUNTY SCHOOL EQUALIZATION FUND", "taxAmt": 0, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 0}]',replace('# ACQUISITION MEMO: PC PEAK DEVELOPMENT\n\n**TO:** Acquisitions Team  \n**RE:** TX-25-01483 - Jamie Cornejo (Life Estate)  \n**DATE:** [Current Date]  \n**PROPERTY:** 1530 E. Overton Rd., Dallas, TX 75216-5506\n\n---\n\n## OWNER SITUATION AND DEBT\n\nTarget owner Jamie Cornejo (a/k/a Jaime Cornejo) holds a life estate interest in the subject property located at 1530 E. Overton Rd., Dallas. This is a tax foreclosure case filed 9/15/2025 in 101st District Court under Judge Carl Ginsberg. Cornejo currently remains **unserved** - citation was attempted via personal service but returned unexecuted on 10/24/2025, indicating possible avoidance or vacancy. Co-defendant Refugio S. Ulloa (same address) was successfully served via Rule 106 substitute service, while Henry Alexander Borg, Jr. (remainder interest holder in Burleson) has been served, retained attorney George Walter McCool, and filed an answer on 10/08/2025. The life estate structure creates complexity, as Cornejo''s interest terminates at death, making this a time-sensitive acquisition opportunity before potential natural expiration of the life estate or forced sale.\n\n## TIMELINE ANALYSIS VS. BENCHMARKS\n\nCase TX-25-01483 is currently **1 month** post-filing with no judgment yet entered. Comparing to benchmark HIGH priority case TX-23-00042 (37 months to judgment, 89 days judgment to OOS), this matter is in extremely early stages. The LOW priority benchmark TX-25-00492 shows 14 months to judgment for simpler cases. **Critical factor:** Borg''s answer filing will likely extend timeline significantly as this creates contested litigation. However, Cornejo''s unserved status may result in default judgment against the life estate interest within 6-9 months if service is eventually perfected via publication. The attorney involvement by one defendant signals sophisticated opposition, suggesting this case will trend closer to the 24-37 month timeline rather than the 14-month baseline.\n\n## ACQUISITION STRATEGY AND OFFER\n\n**Primary approach:** Door-knock campaign at 1530 E. Overton Rd. within next 14 days, targeting weekday evenings (6-8 PM) and Saturday mornings. Given unexecuted service, owner may be present but avoiding process servers - a non-threatening acquisition representative may gain access. **Offer range:** $8,500-$15,000 for life estate release, positioning as','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-05T22:35:40.179856','2026-07-05T23:26:39.123919','2026-07-05T23:26:39.123919',1,'individual','high','',NULL);
INSERT INTO cases VALUES(33,'TX-22-01443','68th District Court, Dallas County, Texas','Carl Ginsberg','2022-09-22','closed','TAX DELINQUENCY','Wilson Charles Chalmers','["Wilson Charles Chalmers", "Alma Ruth Chalmers", "Linda Faye Chalmers a/k/a Linda Sanders", "Vernon Charles Chalmers", "Jo Ann Chalmers a/k/a Jo Ann Booker", "Winston Charles Chalmers", "Veronica Sanders", "Quincy Sanders", "Alicia Sanders"]','2340 Village Way, Dallas, TX 75216-4635',NULL,'00000505255000000','Linebarger Goggan Blair & Sampson, LLP','Ashly S. Atkins',14463.700000000001111,2012,'[2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021]',9,1,0,'["TX-15-01084"]',1,4,2,'Multiple defendants with address unknown at filing; Citation by Posting required for 3 defendants initially; multiple unexecuted citations; non-resident defendant (Alicia Sanders) served via Secretary of State; waiver of service by one defendant (Jo Ann Chalmers)','high','9 defendants; estate/heir situation (Alma Ruth Chalmers deceased with affidavit of heirship filed); multiple defendants with address unknown at filing requiring Citation by Posting; taxes delinquent since 2012 (13 years); prior related suit (TX-15-01084); non-resident defendant served via Secretary of State; 4 continuances; 2 trial resets; multiple ad litem appointments; extensive service complications','2025-09-16','nonjury',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 690.58, "penaltyInterest": 587.3, "total": 1277.88}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 778.69, "penaltyInterest": 666.87, "total": 1445.56}, {"entity": "Dallas County Community College District", "taxAmt": 357.82, "penaltyInterest": 302.06, "total": 659.88}, {"entity": "Dallas County School Equalization Fund", "taxAmt": 28.68, "penaltyInterest": 24.12, "total": 52.8}, {"entity": "Dallas Independent School District", "taxAmt": 3715.64, "penaltyInterest": 3140.39, "total": 6856.03}, {"entity": "City of Dallas", "taxAmt": 2257.15, "penaltyInterest": 1914.4, "total": 4171.55}]',replace('The TX-22-01443 Chalmers case demonstrates HIGH complexity virtually identical to the TX-23-00042 Williams benchmark, with nine defendants versus eight, estate/heir complications involving deceased Alma Ruth Chalmers requiring affidavit of heirship, Citation by Posting for multiple defendants with unknown addresses, and thirteen years of delinquent taxes dating to 2012. The case tracked the Williams benchmark almost perfectly at 37 months filing to judgment (September 2022 to September 2025), matching Williams'' exact 37-month timeline despite having one additional defendant and comparable procedural obstacles including four continuances, two trial resets, three separate ad litem appointments, and non-resident service via Secretary of State for Alicia Sanders. The primary timeline driver was the multi-defendant estate scenario compounded by service complications requiring extended posting periods and multiple attempts to reach heirs, which is precisely the procedural morass that extended Williams from what would otherwise be a 14-month default trajectory like the Hedge benchmark to the full 37-month contested timeline.\n\nThe Order of Sale window projects to mid-December 2025, calculated as 89 days from the September 16, 2025 judgment date based on the Williams benchmark''s confirmed judgment-to-OOS interval. Critical docket watch dates include November 25, 2025 (approximately 70 days post-judgment when OOS issuance typically appears on the docket) and the abstract of judgment filing requested February 4, 2026, which suggests plaintiffs are simultaneously pursuing lien enforcement and preparing for sheriff sale scheduling. This projection would accelerate if defendants file post-judgment motions for new trial (due by September 30, 2025, now past) or if any redemption activity surfaces, though the closed case status, lack of defendant attorney representation beyond ad litem, and notice of judgment mailed September 16, 2025 indicate low probability of post-judgment interference. The timeline would extend only if administrative delays occur at the constable''s office for sale scheduling or if title complications emerge during the sheriff sale preparation process.\n\nAcquisition opportunity is STRONG with immediate action recommended given the property at 2340 Village Way represents a single-family residence in the Deerpath Village subdivision with total judgment exposure of $31,130.47 ($29,542 taxes plus $1,588.47 City of Dallas privileged liens for weed and heavy clean). PC Peak Development should direct counsel to monitor the Dallas County civil docket weekly starting November 18, 2025 for OOS issuance, immediately pull comparable sales data for Deerpath Village Third Installment to establish fair market value against the judgment amount, and prepare a pre-sale title examination to identify any senior liens or encumbrances that survived the tax foreclosure. Specific next steps include engaging a local Dallas title company by November 20, 2025 to run preliminary title work on account number 00000505255000000, establishing bidding authority parameters based on comparable analysis with a target acquisition cost not exceeding 65% of after-repair value given the thirteen-year tax delinquency suggesting potential property condition issues, and assigning an analyst to attend the sheriff sale in person once the sale date posts to assess competitive bidder interest and conduct day-of-sale exterior property condition verification.','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-05T22:35:40.180100','2026-07-05T22:35:40.180112',NULL,1,'individual','high',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO cases VALUES(34,'TX-23-00553','44th District Court, Dallas County, Texas','Carl Ginsberg','2023-03-30','closed','TAX DELINQUENCY','Pauline Hernandez','["Pauline Hernandez", "Norma Hernandez", "Norma E. Baca (In Rem Only)", "Salvador Hernandez, Jr. (In Rem Only)", "Savario Hernandez (In Rem Only)", "Mitza Hernandez (In Rem Only)", "Tavanne S. Salcido (In Rem Only)", "Izumi T. Hernandez (In Rem Only)", "Guisla Z. Hernandez (In Rem Only)", "Aurelio R. Hernandez (In Rem Only)", "Salvador S. Hernandez, III (In Rem Only)", "Lorenzo Hernandez (In Rem Only)"]','2515 West Brooklyn Avenue, Dallas, Dallas County, Texas',NULL,'00000274402000000','Linebarger Goggan Blair & Sampson','Ashly Steele Atkins',75206.559999999997856,2015,'[2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025]',12,1,1,'[]',1,4,4,'Multiple defendants with unknown addresses requiring citation by posting (CBP) for 5 defendants initially; extensive Rule 106 substitute service needed for 4 defendants; multiple unexecuted citations requiring re-service; service complications spanning nearly entire case duration','high','12 defendants (5+ triggers high complexity); citation by posting required at filing for 4 defendants with unknown addresses; extensive estate/heir situation with multiple family members and ''In Rem Only'' designations; 11 years of delinquent taxes (2015-2025); Rule 106 substitute service required for 4 defendants across multiple attempts; 4 continuances and 4 trial resets; attorney ad litem substitution mid-case; extensive service complications throughout 38-month case duration','2026-06-01','nonjury',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 6784.65, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 6784.65}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 7329.03, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 7329.03}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 3476.87, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 3476.87}, {"entity": "Dallas County School Equalization Fund", "taxAmt": 193.24, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 193.24}, {"entity": "Dallas Independent School District", "taxAmt": 35143.01, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 35143.01}, {"entity": "City of Dallas", "taxAmt": 22279.76, "penaltyInterest": 0, "total": 22279.76}]',replace('The TX-23-00553 Hernandez case tracks almost identically to the Williams HIGH complexity benchmark (TX-23-00042), presenting a textbook estate heir situation with extensive service complications that drove a 38-month filing-to-judgment timeline versus Williams'' 37 months. Both cases share the critical complexity drivers: high defendant counts (12 versus 8), citation by posting required at filing for defendants with unknown addresses, decade-plus delinquency spans (11 years versus 21 years), attorney ad litem appointments, and multiple continuances with trial resets (both had exactly 4 trial resets). The key differentiator is that Hernandez actually involved more defendants and required more extensive Rule 106 substitute service across multiple attempts spanning from January 2024 through April 2025, with Mitza Hernandez alone requiring repeated service orders. The mid-case attorney ad litem substitution in February 2026 and the staggered service timeline that extended nearly to trial created incremental delays, but the overall duration remained within one month of the Williams benchmark, confirming that Judge Ginsberg''s docket handles these high-complexity estate cases with remarkable consistency when the same firm (Linebarger Goggan) manages the litigation.\n\nProjecting from the Williams benchmark''s 89-day judgment-to-OOS window, the Hernandez property should reach order of sale approximately late August 2026, with docket watch focused on the 30-day redemption period expiration around July 2, 2026, and subsequent motion for order of sale filing expected mid-July. The critical date to monitor is July 14, 2026 (30 business days post-judgment notice mailed June 2), when plaintiff''s counsel would typically file the motion for order of sale if no redemption occurs. Any deviation from the August 2026 OOS projection would most likely stem from three factors: a defendant filing for bankruptcy protection during the redemption period (particularly Tavanne Salcido, who appeared pro se and demonstrated engagement), an eleventh-hour redemption attempt given the property''s substantial equity position ($271,830 appraised value against $75,206 judgment creates $196,000+ equity cushion that heirs might mobilize to protect), or administrative delays if Linebarger Goggan experiences staffing changes or docket congestion in their Dallas County practice. The notice of judgment was properly mailed to 8 defendants on June 2, 2026, so procedural compliance appears solid, but the large heir group and demonstrated family engagement (one pro se answer, multiple service attempts suggesting family awareness) creates elevated redemption risk compared to the typical abandoned property scenario.\n\nThis represents a strong acquisition opportunity with immediate action required given the compressed timeline between now and the projected August 2026 order of sale. PC Peak Development should instruct counsel to contact Ashly Steele Atkins at Linebarger Goggan this week to express acquisition interest and request notification when the order of sale is signed, as the Williams benchmark demonstrates Judge Ginsberg moves quickly through this final stage once the redemption period expires. Simultaneously, commission a title examination to verify the warranty deed referenced in the legal description (Volume 80169, Page 1084) and confirm no intervening liens or claims were recorded during the 38-month litigation period, particularly focusing on whether any of the 12 defendants recorded homestead affidavits, mechanic''s liens, or other encumbrances that could cloud title post-sale. The 2515 West Brooklyn Avenue location in the Sunset Summit addition warrants immediate physical inspection and comparable sales analysis, as the $271,830 appraised value against only $75,206 in tax debt suggests significant acquisition value, but the 11-year delinquency period raises questions about property condition and potential code violations or demolition orders that could affect development feasibility. Given the one-month window before expected OOS issuance, prioritize speed over perfection: secure the title work and property inspection within 10 business days, prepare bid parameters assuming 10-15% premium over judgment amount to ensure competitive positioning, and establish direct','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-05T22:35:40.180291','2026-07-05T22:35:40.180296',NULL,1,'individual','high',NULL,NULL);
